---
source: worktree/cli/tests/list_table.rs
expression: "labeled(vec![(\"plain\".into(),\nunlinked(\"/code/wts/plain\", Some(\"feat/plain\"))),\n(\"spaces in the path\".into(), unlinked(\"/code/wts/my work\", None)),\n(\"a single quote in the path\".into(), unlinked(\"/code/wts/it's\", None)),\n(\"a PowerShell quote in the path\".into(),\nunlinked(\"/code/wts/it\\u{2019}s\", None)),\n(\"shell metacharacters\".into(), unlinked(\"/code/wts/$(rm -rf ~);x\", None)),\n(\"a leading dash\".into(), unlinked(\"/code/wts/-n\", None)),\n(\"a Windows base path\".into(), unlinked_from_base(\"C:\\\\code\\\\wts\\\\repo\")),\n(\"a UNC base path\".into(), unlinked_from_base(\"\\\\\\\\server\\\\share\\\\repo\")),\n(\"a base path ending in a backslash\".into(),\nunlinked_from_base(\"C:\\\\repo\\\\\")),])"
---
## plain
 - plain: its .git file is missing;  wt remove feat/plain  attempts to restore the link before checking its files. To restore it without removing it, run  git -C /code/wts/repo worktree repair /code/wts/plain .


## spaces in the path
 - my work: its .git file is missing;  wt remove 'my work'  attempts to restore the link before checking its files. To restore it without removing it, run  git -C /code/wts/repo worktree repair '/code/wts/my work' .


## a single quote in the path
 - it's: its .git file is missing; wt remove attempts to restore the link before checking its files. To restore it without removing it, run git worktree repair from the base checkout, naming /code/wts/it's. No name selects it for wt remove: it's can't be typed the same way in every shell.


## a PowerShell quote in the path
 - it’s: its .git file is missing; wt remove attempts to restore the link before checking its files. To restore it without removing it, run git worktree repair from the base checkout, naming /code/wts/it’s. No name selects it for wt remove: it’s can't be typed the same way in every shell.


## shell metacharacters
 - $(rm -rf ~);x: its .git file is missing;  wt remove '$(rm -rf ~);x'  attempts to restore the link before checking its files. To restore it without removing it, run  git -C /code/wts/repo worktree repair '/code/wts/$(rm -rf ~);x' .


## a leading dash
 - -n: its .git file is missing; wt remove attempts to restore the link before checking its files. To restore it without removing it, run  git -C /code/wts/repo worktree repair /code/wts/-n . No name selects it for wt remove: -n can't be typed the same way in every shell.


## a Windows base path
 - plain: its .git file is missing;  wt remove plain  attempts to restore the link before checking its files. To restore it without removing it, run  git -C 'C:\code\wts\repo' worktree repair /code/wts/plain .


## a UNC base path
 - plain: its .git file is missing;  wt remove plain  attempts to restore the link before checking its files. To restore it without removing it, run git worktree repair from the base checkout, naming /code/wts/plain.


## a base path ending in a backslash
 - plain: its .git file is missing;  wt remove plain  attempts to restore the link before checking its files. To restore it without removing it, run git worktree repair from the base checkout, naming /code/wts/plain.
